; SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
;
; tscaly — a Scaly port of the TypeScript compiler.
;
; Ported from microsoft/typescript-go, pinned at commit 2bd066d8 (tag
; typescript/v7.0.2). See ../README.md for provenance and ../CLAUDE.md for the
; working rules — in particular the Go→Scaly mapping vocabulary, which must be
; read before porting a file, and the license boundary (nothing moves from here
; into the MIT parts of this repository).
;
; Memory doctrine, decided at kickoff and to be proven by this port: a compiler
; run is a region hierarchy. The cycles the reference carries — Node.Parent and
; Type.checker pointing back at their owner — cost nothing here, where a cycle
; inside one region is freed with the region. The reference's own memo caches
; already hang off the Checker rather than off globals, so N checkers are N
; regions.
;
; Dispatch doctrine: no dynamic dispatch in the core. The reference's tag-struct
; + interface-payload shape (nodeData, TypeData) becomes a sum type plus pattern
; matching, because a trait object makes the callee unknown at compile time and
; every purity, escape and parallelism question stops there. See CLAUDE.md §3.1.

package scaly 0.1.0

define tscaly
{
    ; The syntax-kind tag. GENERATED — edit tools/genkind.py, not the file.
    ;
    ; It is declared FIRST because module declaration order decides whether a
    ; module-level constant is visible: a `define` read from a module declared
    ; LATER is a hard `unknown identifier` in operator position and, worse, is
    ; SILENTLY DROPPED along with the whole call when it appears as a call
    ; argument. Every module below reads these constants.
    module Kind

    ; Per-token scanner flags. Hand-ported; short and readable.
    module TokenFlags

    ; Per-node parser/binder flags. Hand-ported, like TokenFlags, and declared
    ; here for the same reason Kind is: the parser reads these constants.
    module NodeFlags

    ; The TS error numbers. GENERATED — edit tools/gendiagnostics.py, not the
    ; file. Declared here for the same reason Kind is: both the scanner and the
    ; parser read these constants, and a `define` read from a module declared
    ; LATER is silently dropped in call-argument position.
    module DiagnosticCodes

    ; The parser's diagnostic LIST — shared with the scanner, which is what the
    ; reference's ErrorCallback reduces to here. Declared before the scanner,
    ; which appends to it.
    module Diagnostics

    ; The keyword table + GetIdentifierToken. GENERATED — edit
    ; tools/genkeywords.py, not the file.
    module Keywords

    ; The ECMAScript identifier code-point tables. GENERATED — edit
    ; tools/genunicode.py, not the file. Declared before the scanner, which
    ; calls into it.
    module UnicodeId

    ; The scanner. Everything reachable from Scan() is ported; what remains is
    ; parser-driven (the re-scan entry points, JSX, comment directives) and is
    ; listed at `unported_pos`.
    module scanner

    ; The syntax tree. The reference's tag-struct-plus-interface becomes a
    ; tag-struct plus a SUM TYPE — see CLAUDE.md §3.1 and the file header.
    module ast

    ; The one function of internal/tspath the parser asks for: does this file's
    ; NAME make it a declaration file. Declared before the parser, which calls
    ; it; it reads nothing from any other module.
    module tspath

    ; The parser. Slice 1: the source-file spine, the statements a file of
    ; plain declarations is made of, and primary expressions. Everything else
    ; reports its own position (`unported_pos`) rather than building a tree
    ; that disagrees with the reference while looking well-formed.
    module parser
}
